===============================================================================
1. INSTALLATION
===============================================================================

Since the library is not uploaded to crates.io, add it as a Git dependency in
your Cargo.toml:

  [dependencies]
  librcekunit = { git = "https://codeberg.org/mroczect/librcekunit.git", tag = "v2.0.0" }

To use a specific commit (e.g., for unreleased fixes):

  librcekunit = { git = "https://codeberg.org/mroczect/librcekunit.git", rev = "a1b2c3d" }

For local development (if you have cloned the repository):

  librcekunit = { path = "../librcekunit" }

After adding the dependency, run:

  $ cargo build

The library requires tokio (async runtime). Make sure your application uses
tokio with the `macros` and `rt-multi-thread` features (or full).


===============================================================================
2. FEATURES OVERVIEW
===============================================================================

  +----------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------+
  | Feature                          | Description                                        |
  +----------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------+
  | Cookie management                | In‑memory or persistent file storage (JSON)       |
  | CSRF token handling              | Automatic extraction from HTML and injection      |
  | HTTP methods                     | GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, HEAD, OPTIONS      |
  | Configurable timeout & User‑Agent| Default 30 sec, custom UA string                  |
  | Structured logging               | Via `tracing` – set RUST_LOG env variable         |
  | Comprehensive error types        | Network, I/O, JSON, Auth, API, CSRF, etc.         |
  | Full endpoint coverage           | cekunit, dashboard, PIC, users, input data, etc.  |
  | Export/Import operations         | CSV/JSON export, mass data import                  |
  | Bulk delete                      | Delete all or by category column                   |
  +----------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------+


===============================================================================
3. MODULES AND RE‑EXPORTS (src/lib.rs)
===============================================================================

The library re‑exports the most important types at the crate root:

  • Client         – main API client (from `client::Client`)
  • Config         – configuration struct (from `config`)
  • CookieStore    – cookie persistence enum (from `config`)
  • Error          – unified error type (from `error`)
  • HttpMethod     – HTTP method enum (from `types`)

Additionally, a utility function is available:

  • init_tracing() – initialises the global tracing subscriber.

All other modules are accessible via `librcekunit::module_name`, but most users
will only need the `Client` interface.


===============================================================================
4. STRUCT Config (src/config.rs)
===============================================================================

Configuration container for the HTTP client.

4.1 PUBLIC FIELDS

  +--------------+-----------+-----------------------------------------------+
  | Field        | Type      | Description                                   |
  +--------------+-----------+-----------------------------------------------+
  | base_url     | String    | API root URL, without trailing slash         |
  | timeout      | Duration  | Request timeout (default 30 seconds)         |
  | user_agent   | String    | User‑Agent header (default "librcekunit/2.0")|
  | cookie_store | CookieStore| Cookie persistence policy                     |
  +--------------+-----------+-----------------------------------------------+

4.2 METHODS

  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │ fn from_env() -> Result<Self, Error>                                    │
  ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Reads BASE_URL from environment variable. Also loads .env file if       │
  │ present. Returns Error::Config if BASE_URL is missing.                  │
  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │ fn new(base_url: &str) -> Self                                          │
  ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Creates a Config with default values:                                   │
  │   timeout = 30 seconds                                                  │
  │   user_agent = "librcekunit/2.0"                                        │
  │   cookie_store = CookieStore::Persistent("librcekunit_cookies.json")    │
  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │ fn with_timeout(self, secs: u64) -> Self                                │
  ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Builder‑style setter for timeout (in seconds).                          │
  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │ fn with_user_agent(self, ua: &str) -> Self                              │
  ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Builder‑style setter for the User‑Agent header.                         │
  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │ fn with_cookie_store(self, store: CookieStore) -> Self                  │
  ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Builder‑style setter for cookie storage policy.                         │
  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘


===============================================================================
5. ENUM CookieStore (src/config.rs)
===============================================================================

Determines how cookies are persisted.

  +-------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+
  | Variant     | Behaviour                                                 |
  +-------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+
  | None        | No persistence – cookies are lost when the Client drops. |
  | Memory      | Keep cookies only in memory for the lifetime of Client.  |
  | Persistent  | Save cookies to a JSON file at the given PathBuf.        |
  | (PathBuf)   | Loaded at client creation, saved after every request.    |
  +-------------+-----------------------------------------------------------+


===============================================================================
6. STRUCT Client (src/client.rs)
===============================================================================

Main entry point for all API interactions. Wraps an `HttpClient` and provides
convenience methods for every endpoint.

6.1 CONSTRUCTOR

  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │ async fn new(config: Config) -> Result<Self, Error>                     │
  ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Creates a new Client. Initialises the underlying HTTP client, loads    │
  │ cookies (if persistent), and prepares the CSRF token store.            │
  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

6.2 AUTHENTICATION METHODS

  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │ async fn login(&self, email: &str, password: &str) -> Result<(), Error> │
  ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Performs a full login workflow:                                         │
  │   1. Fetches CSRF token from `/login` page.                             │
  │   2. Submits credentials with the token.                                │
  │   3. On success, resets the internal CSRF token (session established). │
  │ Returns Error::Auth for invalid credentials.                            │
  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │ async fn logout(&self) -> Result<(), Error>                             │
  ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Sends POST to `/logout`, clears persistent cookie file (if any) and    │
  │ resets the CSRF token.                                                  │
  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

6.3 LOW‑LEVEL ACCESS

  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │ fn http(&self) -> &HttpClient                                           │
  ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Returns a reference to the internal HttpClient (for advanced use).     │
  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │ async fn request(&self, method: HttpMethod, path: &str,                 │
  │                  body: Option<HashMap<String, String>>)                 │
  │                  -> Result<reqwest::Response, Error>                    │
  ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Generic request builder. For GET/HEAD the body becomes query params;   │
  │ for others it becomes form data. CSRF token is automatically added     │
  │ to non‑GET requests.                                                    │
  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

6.4 ENDPOINT METHODS (all async, return Result<reqwest::Response, Error>)

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  DASHBOARD
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  • dashboard_index()
  • dashboard_index_with_params(params: HashMap<String, String>)

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  CEKUNIT (basic CRUD)
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  • cekunit_index()
  • cekunit_index_with_params(params)
  • cekunit_create()
  • cekunit_store(data: HashMap<String, String>)
  • cekunit_show(no: u64)
  • cekunit_edit(no: u64)
  • cekunit_update(no: u64, data)
  • cekunit_destroy(no: u64)

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  DASHBOARD ACTIONS (bulk operations)
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  • dashboard_delete_all()
  • cekunit_delete_by_category(column: &str, value: &str)
  • cekunit_export(format: &str, sort: &str, direction: &str)
  • cekunit_get_unique_values(column: &str)

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  INPUT USER (full CRUD + export/import)
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  • input_user_index()
  • input_user_index_with_params(params)
  • input_user_create()
  • input_user_store(data)
  • input_user_show(id: u64)
  • input_user_edit(id: u64)
  • input_user_update(id: u64, data)
  • input_user_destroy(id: u64)
  • input_user_export(params: HashMap<String, String>)
  • input_user_import(data: HashMap<String, String>)

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  INPUT DATA (create only)
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  • input_data_create()
  • input_data_store(data)

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  PIC (Person In Charge)
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  • pic_index()
  • pic_index_with_params(params)
  • pic_create()
  • pic_store(data)
  • pic_show(nomor: u64)
  • pic_edit(nomor: u64)
  • pic_update(nomor: u64, data)
  • pic_destroy(nomor: u64)
  • dashboard_pic_index()
  • dashboard_pic_index_with_params(params)
  • input_pic_create()
  • input_pic_store(data)

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  USERS
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  • users_index()
  • users_index_with_params(params)
  • users_create()
  • users_store(data)
  • users_show(nomor: u64)
  • users_edit(nomor: u64)
  • users_update(nomor: u64, data)
  • users_destroy(nomor: u64)
  • dashboard_users_index()
  • dashboard_users_index_with_params(params)


===============================================================================
7. STRUCT HttpClient (src/http_client.rs)
===============================================================================

Internal HTTP client. Not exported directly, but accessible via
`Client::http()`. It manages cookie jars, CSRF tokens, and request building.

PUBLIC METHODS (available through the reference):

  +--------------------------+-----------------------------------------------+
  | Method                   | Description                                   |
  +--------------------------+-----------------------------------------------+
  | fn base_url(&self) -> &str                                          |
  | fn cookie_jar(&self) -> &Arc<Jar>                                   |
  | async fn fetch_csrf_token(&self, url: &str) -> Result<String, Error>|
  | fn parse_csrf_from_html(html: &str) -> Result<String, Error>        |
  | async fn set_csrf_token(&self, token: String)                       |
  | async fn get_csrf_token(&self) -> Option<String>                    |
  | async fn request(...) -> Result<reqwest::Response, Error>           |
  | async fn clear_session(&self)                                       |
  | async fn reset_csrf_token(&self)                                    |
  +--------------------------+-----------------------------------------------+


===============================================================================
8. ENUM Error (src/error.rs)
===============================================================================

All errors that can be returned by the library.

  +------------------+-----------------------------------------------------+
  | Variant          | Description                                         |
  +------------------+-----------------------------------------------------+
  | Config(String)   | Configuration error (e.g., BASE_URL missing)       |
  | Reqwest(reqwest::Error) | Network / HTTP error                         |
  | Io(std::io::Error)      | Filesystem I/O error                         |
  | Json(serde_json::Error) | JSON serialization/deserialization error     |
  | Auth(String)      | Authentication failure (invalid credentials)       |
  | Api(u16, String)  | API returned an HTTP error (status code, message)  |
  | CsrfNotFound      | CSRF token not found in HTML response              |
  | NotLoggedIn       | Attempt to access protected endpoint without login|
  | CookieStore(String)| Cookie persistence error (e.g., file write fail)  |
  +------------------+-----------------------------------------------------+

All variants implement `std::error::Error` and `std::fmt::Display` via `thiserror`.


===============================================================================
9. MODULE types (src/types.rs)
===============================================================================

9.1 ENUM HttpMethod

  Variants: GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, HEAD, OPTIONS

  Methods:
    • fn as_str(&self) -> &'static str
    • Implements Display (so `to_string()` works)

9.2 FUNCTION join_url(base: &str, path: &str) -> String

  Joins a base URL and a path, handling duplicate slashes. If `path` starts
  with "http", it is returned as‑is (absolute URL).

9.3 STRUCT ApiResponse<T>

  Generic wrapper for JSON API responses.

  Fields:
    • status: String      – typically "success" or "error"
    • data: Option<T>     – payload if present
    • message: Option<String> – optional human‑readable message

  Implements Serialize and Deserialize from serde.


===============================================================================
10. MODULE cookies (src/cookies.rs)
===============================================================================

Low‑level functions to save/load cookies from a JSON file. Usually not needed
directly because `HttpClient` handles persistence automatically.

  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │ fn save_cookies_to_file(jar: &Jar, url: &str, path: &Path)              │
  │   -> Result<(), Error>                                                  │
  ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Saves all cookies from the jar that match the given URL to a JSON file. │
  │ If no cookies exist, the file is removed.                               │
  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │ fn load_cookies_from_file(jar: &Jar, url: &str, path: &Path)            │
  │   -> Result<(), Error>                                                  │
  ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Loads cookies from a JSON file into the jar. If the file does not       │
  │ exist, returns Ok(()) without error.                                    │
  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

Both functions panic if the URL string cannot be parsed (this should not happen
with a valid base URL from `Config`).


===============================================================================
11. MODULE api (src/api/*.rs)
===============================================================================

These raw functions are used internally by `Client`. They accept an
`&HttpClient` and provide endpoint‑specific requests. You may use them directly
if you have a custom `HttpClient` instance, but the recommended way is to use
`Client` methods.

All functions have the same signature pattern:

  async fn endpoint_name(client: &HttpClient, ...) -> Result<reqwest::Response, Error>

For brevity, only the names are listed below. See the source code or the
`Client` method documentation for exact parameters.

11.1 api::auth
  • login(client, email, password) -> Result<(), Error>
  • logout(client) -> Result<(), Error>

11.2 api::crud (cekunit)
  • index, index_with_params, create, store, show, edit, update, destroy

11.3 api::dashboard
  • dashboard_index, dashboard_index_with_params, delete_all, delete_by_category,
    export, get_unique_values

11.4 api::input_data
  • create, store

11.5 api::input_user
  • index, index_with_params, create, store, show, edit, update, destroy,
    export, import

11.6 api::pic
  • index, index_with_params, create, store, show, edit, update, destroy,
    dashboard_index, dashboard_index_with_params, input_create, input_store

11.7 api::users
  • index, index_with_params, create, store, show, edit, update, destroy,
    dashboard_index, dashboard_index_with_params


===============================================================================
12. UTILITY FUNCTION init_tracing (src/lib.rs)
===============================================================================

  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │ fn init_tracing()                                                       │
  ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Initialises the global `tracing` subscriber with a formatted writer    │
  │ and an env filter. The log level can be set via the `RUST_LOG`         │
  │ environment variable. Default level is "info".                          │
  │                                                                         │
  │ Example:                                                                │
  │   $ RUST_LOG=debug cargo run                                            │
  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘


===============================================================================
13. COMPLETE USAGE EXAMPLES
===============================================================================

13.1 Basic login and data retrieval

  use librcekunit::{Client, Config};
  use std::collections::HashMap;

  #[tokio::main]
  async fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
      librcekunit::init_tracing();

      let config = Config::from_env()
          .unwrap_or_else(|_| Config::new("http://localhost:8080"))
          .with_timeout(30);

      let client = Client::new(config).await?;

      // Login
      client.login("admin@example.com", "password123").await?;

      // Get first page of cekunit data
      let resp = client.cekunit_index().await?;
      println!("GET /cekunit -> status {}", resp.status());

      // Query with parameters
      let mut params = HashMap::new();
      params.insert("page".to_string(), "2".to_string());
      params.insert("sort".to_string(), "id".to_string());
      let resp = client.cekunit_index_with_params(params).await?;

      client.logout().await?;
      Ok(())
  }

13.2 Creating a new input data record

  let mut data = HashMap::new();
  data.insert("no_perjanjian".into(), "OD-26-F0000999".into());
  data.insert("nama_nasabah".into(), "Budi Santoso".into());
  data.insert("nopol".into(), "B 1234 ABC".into());
  data.insert("kategori".into(), "A".into());
  data.insert("status".into(), "JG".into());

  match client.input_data_store(data).await {
      Ok(resp) if resp.status().is_success() => println!("Created"),
      Ok(resp) => eprintln!("HTTP error: {}", resp.status()),
      Err(e) => eprintln!("Request failed: {}", e),
  }

13.3 Exporting input users as CSV with date filters

  let mut params = HashMap::new();
  params.insert("format".into(), "csv".into());
  params.insert("start_date".into(), "2026-01-01".into());
  params.insert("end_date".into(), "2026-12-31".into());
  params.insert("sort".into(), "created_at".into());

  let resp = client.input_user_export(params).await?;
  let content = resp.bytes().await?;
  std::fs::write("export.csv", content)?;

13.4 Handling authentication errors

  match client.login("user@example.com", "wrong").await {
      Ok(()) => println!("OK"),
      Err(Error::Auth(msg)) => eprintln!("Login failed: {}", msg),
      Err(e) => eprintln!("Other error: {}", e),
  }

13.5 Using the low‑level request method

  use librcekunit::HttpMethod;

  let resp = client.request(
      HttpMethod::GET,
      "/some/custom/endpoint",
      Some([("key", "value")].iter().map(|(k,v)| (k.to_string(), v.to_string())).collect())
  ).await?;


